<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diego López V de Haro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1310</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diego López V de Haro was lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biscay">Biscay</a> and one of the leading nobles of the Crown of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, a member of the powerful Haro family. In 1300 he granted a town charter to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bilbao">Bilbao</a>, founding the city that became Biscay's chief port. He died in 1310 during the Castilian siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeciras">Algeciras</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diego-lopez-v-de-haro.jpg" alt="Diego López V de Haro" width="320" height="585" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fernando Pascullo · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Don_Diego_L%C3%B3pez_de_Haro_V.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
